   "source": [
    "### Public Transport Dataset (Houston, SF and NY) (#4)\n",
    "\n",
    "This dataset contains counts of unlinked passenger trips (ridership) for public transit in Houston, San Fransisco, and New York, covering the years 2002 through 2025. The data is sourced from the Federal Transit Administration's (FTA) National Transit Database (NTD) Monthly Ridership module. The key metrics are:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Year**: the calendar year the ridership was recorded.\n",
    "- **Ridership**: the total number of unlinked passenger trips across all transit modes and service types operated in the city\n",
    "- **City**: the city the ridership data corresponds to (Houston, SF or NY).\n",
    "\n",
    "**Note**: Ridership figures are aggregated across all modes (e.g. Motorbus, Commuter Bus, Demand Response, Light Rail) and all types of service (Directly Operated and Purchased Transportation). NaN values in the raw data indicate a mode/service type was not yet operational or not reported in that year — these are treated as zero in the aggregation. A significant ridership drop is observed in 2020-2021 due to the COVID-19 pandemic, and figures have not fully recovered to pre-pandemic levels as of 2025."
   ]
  },
