    "### New York Asthma Dataset\n",
    "\n",
    "This is the dataset of adults(18+) reporting an asthma diagnosis, and symptoms, in the last 12 months (from when they were surveyed) in New York city. The data collected for this dataset include the following areas in New York city: the Bronx, Manhattan, Brooklyn, Staten Island, and Queens. It includes the number of population and percentage of reported adults from 2003-2022, and the data is collected per year.\n",
    "- **TimePeriod**: the year the data is collected\n",
    "- **GeoTypeDesc**: citywide or borough for different areas.\n",
    "- **GeoID**: the id used by the source to identify 1: citywide and Bronx, 2: Brooklyn, 3: Manhattan, 4: Queens, 5: Staten Island.\n",
    "- **BoroID**: the ID for only the borough, 1: Bronx, 2: Brooklyn, 3: Manhattan, 4: Queens, 5: Staten Island.\n",
    "- **Geography**: text data including the following different regions: New York City wide, Bronx, Brooklyn, Manhattan, Queens, Staten Island.\n",
    "- **Area**: the same as Geography.\n",
    "- **Number**: estimated number of adults aged 18 years and older who reported medically diagnosed asthma and symptoms in the last 12 months, rounded to the nearest 1,000. Beginning in 2017, indicator includes data imputed for missing responses.\n",
    "- **Percent**: estimated number of adults aged 18 years and older who reported medically diagnosed asthma with symptoms in the last 12 months, divided by all adults; expressed as percent. Beginning in 2017, indicator includes data imputed for missing responses.\n",
    "- **Age-adjusted percent**: estimated number of adults aged 18 years and older who reported medically diagnosed asthma with symptoms in the last 12 months, divided by all adults and adjusted for age; expressed as percent. Beginning in 2017, indicator includes data imputed for missing responses."
   ]
  },
