   "source": [
    "### San Francisco Asthma Dataset\n",
    "\n",
    "This is the CHIS Data-Current Asthma Prevalence by County 2015-Present dataset. This dataset contains current asthma prevalence, the estimated percentage of Californians who have ever been diagnosed with asthma by a health care provider AND report they still have asthma and/or had an asthma episode or attack within the past 12 months, statewide and by county. The data are stratified by age group (all ages, 0-17, 18+, 0-4, 5-17, 18-64, 65+) and reported for 2-year periods. These data are derived from the California Health Interview Survey (CHIS).\n",
    "\n",
    "- **County**: the county of residence\n",
    "- **Years**: 2-year period during which survey data were collected\n",
    "- **Strata**: general demographic category under which responses have been stratified\n",
    "- **Age Group**: all ages, 0-17 years, 18+ years, 0-4 years, 5-17 years, 18-64 years, and 65+ years\n",
    "- **Current Prevalence**: estimate of the percentage of people who report that they have ever been diagnosed with asthma AND that they still have asthma at the time of the survey (source: CHIS)\n",
    "- **95% Confidence Interval**: the current prevalence estimate is calculated from survey respondents (who represent a sample of the population) and may not reflect the true current prevalence for the entire population. This 95% confidence interval is the range of values which contains the popuation's actual current prevalence with 95% certainty\n",
    "- **Counties Grouped**: counties combined for analysis\n",
    "- **Comment**: warning provided when prevalence estimate is statistically unstable (standard error is 30-50% of prevalence estimate). Data suppressed when standard error exceeds 50% of prevalence estimate\n"
   ]
