    "#### Vehicle Registrations EDA\n",
    "\n",
    "This section explores vehicle registration data across three cities — Houston, San Francisco, and New York City — over time. The dataset breaks down registrations by fuel type (Electric, Hybrid, Diesel, Flex, and Gasoline) as both raw counts and percentage share of total registered vehicles.\n",
    "\n",
    "Since our central argument concerns EV adoption, percentage share is the primary metric used throughout. Raw counts can be misleading given the significant difference in city population and total vehicle registrations, so normalizing by share allows for a fair city-to-city comparison.\n",
    "\n",
    "We begin by defining consistent color schemes for both cities and fuel types, which will be reused across all plots in this section."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "## YOUR CODE HERE\n",
