    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "FUEL_COLORS = {\n",
    "    'Electric': '#2ecc71',   # green\n",
    "    'Hybrid':   '#3498db',   # blue\n",
    "    'Diesel':   '#e67e22',   # orange\n",
    "    'Flex':     '#9b59b6',   # purple\n",
    "    'Gasoline': '#95a5a6',   # grey (de-emphasized)\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "EV_COLOR = \"#2ecc71\"\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "We start with a broad view of how fuel type composition has shifted across all three cities. Gasoline is excluded here to better surface the trends in alternative fuels — its dominance (80%+) would otherwise compress everything else into near-invisible slivers. Each panel shows around the same time range, with a shared y-axis for direct comparison."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
