    "### Exploratory Data Analysis: Smoking Prevalence Trends (2002–2024)\n",
    "This analysis examines the decline of adult smoking prevalence across three major US urban centers: Houston (Harris County), San Francisco, and New York City.\n",
    "\n",
    "The goal of this EDA is to:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Visualize Temporal Trends: Compare the trajectory of smoking cessation across different geographic and policy environments.\n",
    "\n",
    "2. Assess Data Quality: Identify how the exclusion of \"statistically unstable\" data points (primarily in the SF dataset) impacts the continuity of the trend lines.\n",
    "\n",
    "3. Cross-City Comparison: Determine if the cities are converging toward a similar smoking rate or if local factors maintain significant disparities."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 27,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
